WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.312
Before a protein takes shape, transfer RNA helps turn genetic

00:00:05.312 --> 00:00:10.073
instructions into an amino-acid sequence. It is not passive cellular plumbing.

00:00:14.383 --> 00:00:19.605
tRNA charging, chemical modification, cleavage and localisation create

00:00:19.605 --> 00:00:24.826
several different biological functions and possible intervention points.

00:00:29.425 --> 00:00:33.933
Aminoacyl-tRNA synthetases have catalytic charging functions, and

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:38.441
some have additional signalling roles beyond translation.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:47.180
Disrupting universally needed translation can injure healthy cells.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.810
A drug programme must demonstrate a disease-specific vulnerability.

00:00:56.008 --> 00:01:01.061
An enzyme pocket, disease-associated RNA fragment or extracellular

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:06.113
synthetase domain requires different chemistry, assays and delivery.

00:01:10.592 --> 00:01:15.407
The column argues for testing the exact molecular dependency rather

00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:20.222
than declaring the entire tRNA system either undruggable or safe.
